From 460a96fc7345b5aa55b9247b12ff0b2ea7b7b513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Felipe Strano Moraes <luis.strano@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:32:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Support optional zero-run encoded PS1 textures

Keep encoded TIM blobs in resident storage and unpack into a caller-owned, word-aligned upload buffer. Raw descriptors remain the default; encoded uploads validate stream and TIM chunk bounds before GPU commands. Synchronize uploads before reusing scratch during palette resolution.

Cover exact decoding, run limits, malformed streams, overlapping buffers, insufficient scratch, shared palettes, residency aliases and queued-DMA lifetimes in a portable runtime test.
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt                            |   6 +
 .../ps1/starter/runtime/texture_unpack.h      |  33 +++++
 templates/ps1/starter/runtime/textures.c      |  47 ++++++-
 templates/ps1/starter/runtime/textures.h      |   7 +
 tests/Ps1TextureUnpackTests.c                 | 127 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 218 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 templates/ps1/starter/runtime/texture_unpack.h
 create mode 100644 tests/Ps1TextureUnpackTests.c

